# The github.com/jack-work/msauth revision this client's source requires.
#
# goop links the foundation as a Go LIBRARY, so an installed binary freezes
# whatever foundation existed when it was built and inherits no later fix until
# someone rebuilds it. That is the whole reason this file exists: between
# 2026-07-28 and 2026-08-02 the foundation's convergence was declared five times
# and reached exactly one of its five clients -- the only one that execs the
# shared binary instead of linking it.
#
# TestInstalledArtifactCarriesTheRequiredFoundation judges the installed
# artifact against this floor, reading its build metadata without running it.
# An artifact carrying this revision OR ANY LATER ONE passes.
#
# Raise this when goop starts depending on something newer, then rebuild and
# reinstall so the gate goes green again:
#
#   STAMP=$(git -C ../msauth rev-parse --short HEAD)
#   [ -z "$(git -C ../msauth status --porcelain)" ] || STAMP="$STAMP+dirty"
#   go build -ldflags "-X github.com/jack-work/msauth.Stamp=$STAMP" -o loop.exe .
#
# Write those as two statements. The tidier one-liner exits 1 on a clean tree.
#
# This file holds one revision and comments. It must never hold a filesystem
# path: this repository is public, and an install path here names its author.
29679c9
